WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.206
"Mowgli is probably okay, Baloo," Bagheera said.

2
00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:10.083
"He's smart and you've taught him well."

3
00:00:10.084 --> 00:00:14.000
Bagheera licked a paw thoughtfully.

4
00:00:14.001 --> 00:00:18.503
"But we do need a plan to get him back."

5
00:00:18.504 --> 00:00:21.686
"Well, that's a problem," Baloo said.

6
00:00:21.687 --> 00:00:27.819
"Because those monkeys aren't scared of either one of us. Hey!"

7
00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:30.254
He sat up with a jerk.

8
00:00:30.255 --> 00:00:36.292
"The monkeys are afraid of Kaa. Let's go talk to him!"

9
00:00:36.293 --> 00:00:39.553
"I don't really like talking to the python.

10
00:00:39.554 --> 00:00:45.584
I'm not sure he's our friend. And . . ." Bagheera shuddered.

11
00:00:45.585 --> 00:00:49.073
"He has spooky eyes."

12
00:00:49.074 --> 00:00:52.595
"Come on, Bagheera. Kaa is very cunning.

13
00:00:52.596 --> 00:00:55.166
Let's go see if he can help us."

14
00:00:55.167 --> 00:01:01.315
Bagheera sighed. "Fine."

15
00:01:01.316 --> 00:01:05.586
*** Kaa lay on a warm rock in the afternoon

16
00:01:05.587 --> 00:01:09.970
sun. His long body was twisted into coils and

17
00:01:09.971 --> 00:01:16.087
curves. He was admiring his new brown and yellow

18
00:01:16.088 --> 00:01:22.229
skin. "Be careful, Bagheera," Baloo whispered as they

19
00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:27.048
approached. "Kaa is always a little blind after he has changed his skin.

20
00:01:27.049 --> 00:01:30.082
This makes him quick to strike."

21
00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:37.430
Kaa was not a poisonous snake, but he was still very dangerous.

22
00:01:37.431 --> 00:01:42.733
He could coil tightly around someone in a deadly squeeze.

23
00:01:42.734 --> 00:01:47.811
"Good day, Kaa!" Baloo called.

24
00:01:47.812 --> 00:01:56.741
"Oh, Baloo, what are you doing here?"

25
00:01:56.742 --> 00:02:00.848
"We came to ask for your help," the bear replied.

26
00:02:00.849 --> 00:02:05.721
"We need to find the monkeys. It's a bit of an emergency."

27
00:02:05.722 --> 00:02:11.092
"Sss." Kaa let out a lazy hiss.

28
00:02:11.093 --> 00:02:18.550
"I'm tired and full. I'm in no mood to chase monkeys right now."

29
00:02:18.551 --> 00:02:21.463
Baloo flashed a look at Bagheera.

30
00:02:21.464 --> 00:02:24.932
What if Kaa wouldn't help them?

31
00:02:24.933 --> 00:02:29.313
"Um, Kaa . . ." Bagheera swallowed.

32
00:02:29.314 --> 00:02:35.855
"Did you know that the monkeys call you a footless yellow earthworm?"

33
00:02:35.856 --> 00:02:38.912
Kaa's eyes flashed with anger.

34
00:02:38.913 --> 00:02:42.381
"They call me an earthworm

35
00:02:42.382 --> 00:02:46.522
?" "Something like that," Bagheera

36
00:02:46.523 --> 00:02:51.211
replied. "And sometimes they make fun of you," Baloo chimed

37
00:02:51.212 --> 00:02:58.029
in. "They say you have no teeth. And you're afraid of goats'

38
00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:03.024
horns." "What?" Kaa coiled up

39
00:03:03.025 --> 00:03:08.112
tightly. The big swallowing muscles on his throat rippled and

40
00:03:08.113 --> 00:03:12.021
bulged. "Why are you looking for the

41
00:03:12.022 --> 00:03:17.259
monkeys?" "Well, as you know, I am the man cub's teacher," Baloo

42
00:03:17.268 --> 00:03:21.239
began. "He usually listens to me, but once,

43
00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:23.552
he—" Bagheera was getting

44
00:03:23.553 --> 00:03:28.382
impatient. They didn't have time for long

45
00:03:28.383 --> 00:03:31.991
stories. "The trouble is this, Kaa," he said, jumping

46
00:03:31.992 --> 00:03:36.405
in. "Those silly nut-stealers have stolen away the man

47
00:03:36.406 --> 00:03:40.191
cub." "He's a wonderful man cub," Baloo

48
00:03:40.192 --> 00:03:45.584
said. "Mowgli is the smartest and boldest of all the man cubs in the

49
00:03:45.585 --> 00:03:50.367
world. I—we—love him,

50
00:03:50.368 --> 00:03:55.416
Kaa." "Ssss!" Kaa wove his head back and

51
00:03:55.417 --> 00:04:02.924
forth. "The man cub belongs with you—not those monkeys. You are his

52
00:04:02.925 --> 00:04:05.583
family." "That's why we're here," Bagheera

53
00:04:05.584 --> 00:04:10.968
said. "The monkeys are afraid of only one animal in the jungle—you."

54
00:04:10.969 --> 00:04:18.066
"So we're hoping you'll help us find them," Baloo added. "Please."

55
00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:24.184
"Those horrible monkeys chatter constantly," Kaa muttered.

56
00:04:24.185 --> 00:04:27.873
"And they are foolish and lazy."

57
00:04:27.874 --> 00:04:30.487
He swung toward Bagheera.

58
00:04:30.488 --> 00:04:34.867
"What do the monkeys call me—a yellow fish?"

59
00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:37.257
Bagheera lowered his head.

60
00:04:37.258 --> 00:04:43.111
"A yellow earthworm. And other terrible names."

61
00:04:43.112 --> 00:04:49.162
"I'm going to remind them to speak well of me!" Kaa snapped.

62
00:04:49.163 --> 00:04:51.959
"Where did they go?"

63
00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:55.973
"We thought you might know, Kaa," Baloo said.

64
00:04:55.974 --> 00:05:02.688
"I do know they moved to a different part of the jungle today." Kaa hissed.

65
00:05:02.689 --> 00:05:08.504
"I heard them laughing among the treetops earlier. But I—"

66
00:05:08.505 --> 00:05:13.160
"Up! Up!" A sharp cry came from above.

67
00:05:13.161 --> 00:05:18.990
Baloo looked up. Rann was flying across the sky.

68
00:05:18.991 --> 00:05:22.754
"I have a message from Mowgli!" the hawk cried.

69
00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:25.966
"The monkeys have carried him deep into the jungle.

70
00:05:25.967 --> 00:05:32.732
He is now beyond the river—in Monkey City!"

